{
  "about": "#691: a multi-part design drawn part by part, each part in its own colour. The companion writes current.parts (and each sealed version's result.parts) when the printer MCP meshes a 3MF's parts (counterpart/1 counterpart_part_meshes, services/printer-handoff/src/model-parts.ts): [{id, name?, colour?, plate?, painted?, mesh}], id the MCP's key (never parsed), mesh a project path to that part's STL in the 3MF's build frame in millimetres (all parts line up drawn together; parts on plate 2 and later lie at that plate's offset), colour #RRGGBB (the pass's declared colour, else the 3MF's own), plate the 0-based plate (absent for a plain 3MF), painted when the part carries painting (colour is then its base filament's). Without parts (an MCP without the tool, a one-colour model) nothing changes: the stage turns the merged mesh in the neutral material, as today, named as project-gallery.json names it: a 3MF design's mergedMesh (current/model.stl), and an STL design's current model as model.stl, the companion's alias for it (GET /v1/objects/<id>/model.stl). Every client (CounterpartKit, Android, Linux) reads each case: draw is what the stage turns for the design shown, in order, each mesh with its colour, or \"neutral\" for none. A designer's kit draws only the chosen plate's parts (publishedSelection.plateIndex); parts with no plate are on every plate. The companion's own test (services/companion/tests/objects-parts.test.mjs) writes the first two cases' records. Every record here has the fields a real one carries (current.renders; a sealed version's sealedAtMs and modelSha256), so a client decodes it as it decodes the companion's.",
